- Per-source failures (directory source, missing source, unwritable dest, self-copy) are diagnosed and the loop continues.
- New files are created with `open(O_CREAT)` passing source rwx bits; the kernel applies the process umask (022 from the test harness). Existing destinations are opened with `O_WRONLY|O_TRUNC` preserving their existing permissions.
- No heap allocation, no subprocesses, no external utilities. Fixed 64 KiB stack buffer for the copy loop.
- `EINTR` is handled in both `read` and `write` loops.
- All file descriptors are closed on every exit path from `copy_path`.

